"""The row schedule under row sharding is ONE schedule on every rank: the free device bytes it derives from are agreed across ranks
(opt_core.mem.rowpair.dist.agreed_free_bytes: min over ranks) before trimul's RA / RB are chosen. (a) At world size 1 / without a group
the selection is 0.4.1's, value for value (recorded fixtures below were generated by 0.4.1's ``default_rows_a`` / ``default_rows_b``); (b) two gloo
ranks that see UNEQUAL free bytes (mocked) choose the same RA / RB, complete both contractions and match the dense statement."""
